# The G1 stone floor under G5's checks. orphans: its moss flecks were single pixels of four
# different tones (9,0 3,1 14,6 15,6 16,6 17,6 4,14 3,15 4,15 7,15 20,18 20,21; pairs 5,14 4,16).
# Each becomes a small clump of one or two tones.
px 9,0 c=moss1
px 3,1 c=stone3
px 14,6 c=stone3
px 15,6 16,6 17,6 c=moss3
px 4,14 5,14 3,15 4,15 c=moss2
px 6,15 7,15 c=moss1
px 4,16 c=moss0
px 20,18 20,21 c=moss1
# seam: the tile's top and bottom rows ran along a course of stone tops, a line at every seam.
# Moving the courses down 4 rows puts the seam inside the stones.
shift 0,4 wrap
